window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b104-6f10a03feb15baf4.json"]={sha256:"6f10a03feb15baf43cb0bf024f0973a5a4117d1a358a42edd532e245ddcd63a4",value:{"id":"b104","title":"勒奇山基線隧道","titleEn":"Lotschberg Base Tunnel","category":"underground","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"勒奇山案例的核心不是單純延長隧道，而是已營運路線如何面對分期建造留下的容量與介面限制。BLS公開資料將其描述為約35公里的基線隧道；本課把未裝設段、單線衝突、維修窗口、出水與施工隔離分開，逐步建立可供營運和擴建共同審查的證據鏈。","summaryEn":"The Lotschberg case concerns the capacity and interfaces left by staged construction rather than length alone. BLS describes an approximately 35 km base tunnel. This course separates unfinished bore sections, single-track conflicts, maintenance windows, water conditions and construction isolation, building an evidence chain that operations and expansion teams can review together.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"ug-landmarks","subcategoryTitle":"世界隧道與地下巨作","subcategoryTitleEn":"World tunnels and underground landmarks","learningTrack":"underground","learningSubdiscipline":"ug-landmarks","learningTags":["underground","ug-landmarks","tunnel"],"architectureFamily":"tunnel","architectureNodes":[["路線里程與端點","Alignment chainage and endpoints"],["區段占用時間","Section occupation time"],["測壓水頭","Piezometric head"],["出渣運輸節拍","Muck-transport cycle"],["風道摩擦壓損","Duct friction loss"],["資產資料完整度","Asset-record completeness"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,5],[1,5]],"diagram":{"type":"tunnel","labels":["路線里程與端點","區段占用時間","測壓水頭","出渣運輸節拍","風道摩擦壓損"],"labelsEn":["Alignment chainage and endpoints","Section occupation time","Piezometric head","Muck-transport cycle","Duct friction loss"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創綜合審查：先計算「單線瓶頸與時距容量」，再獨立計算「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」。原創教學假設：區段占用=15 min；清空餘裕=2 min。C=60/(tocc+tclear)=3.52941 trains/h。僅把區段占用增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為3.24324 trains/h。邊界：單方向理論容量，未含對向衝突、延誤或維修；不是本工程實測或允收值。原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=23 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=157.714 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為143.377 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。兩組結果的單位與邊界不同，不能直接相加。請列出一項缺少的現場輸入，說明它會影響哪個結論，以及哪種獨立量測可以縮小不確定度。","textEn":"Original integrated review: first calculate single-track bottlenecks and headway capacity, then independently calculate shared access and transport bottlenecks. Original teaching assumptions: occupation=15 min; clearance=2 min. C=60/(tocc+tclear)=3.52941 trains/h. Increasing only occupation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 3.24324 trains/h. Boundary: One-direction theoretical capacity without opposing conflicts, delay or maintenance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=23 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=157.714 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 143.377 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. The outputs have different units and boundaries and cannot simply be added. Identify one missing field input, explain which conclusion it changes and select an independent measurement to reduce uncertainty.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":14,"enrichmentVersion":14,"stages":[{"id":"b104-v14-s1","title":"地層條件、邊界與工程系統","titleEn":"Ground conditions, boundaries and engineering system","description":"本階段聚焦「服務邊界與路線代價」與「單線瓶頸與時距容量」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" and \"Single-track bottlenecks and headway capacity\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b104-v14-01","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「路線里程與端點」如何影響勒奇山基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alignment chainage and endpoints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Lotschberg Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"比較勒奇山已營運段與擴建段的共同端點，將未裝軌洞體與不存在的洞段分開，避免把土建完成當交通容量。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「路線里程與端點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare common endpoints across operating and expansion sections, distinguishing an unfitted bore from an unexcavated section before assigning transport capacity. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk. Compare options between identical endpoints and distinguish running bores, approaches and service galleries. Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alignment chainage and endpoints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：長度=13.2 km；速度=60 km/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: length=13.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=13.2 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「路線里程與端點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alignment chainage and endpoints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-01-k1","title":"服務邊界與路線代價","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost","text":"比較勒奇山已營運段與擴建段的共同端點，將未裝軌洞體與不存在的洞段分開，避免把土建完成當交通容量。隧道選線同時改變洞口、覆土與縱坡，短路線不保證低地質風險。","textEn":"Compare common endpoints across operating and expansion sections, distinguishing an unfitted bore from an unexcavated section before assigning transport capacity. Alignment changes portals, cover and gradient together, so a shorter tunnel need not have lower geological risk.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" is correct?","options":["最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","比較勒奇山已營運段與擴建段的共同端點，將未裝軌洞體與不存在的洞段分開，避免把土建完成當交通容量。","單向理論列車數可以直接當作雙向可承諾營運容量。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","Compare common endpoints across operating and expansion sections, distinguishing an unfitted bore from an unexcavated section before assigning transport capacity.","One-direction theoretical train count can be promised as two-way operational capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"比較勒奇山已營運段與擴建段的共同端點，將未裝軌洞體與不存在的洞段分開，避免把土建完成當交通容量。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare common endpoints across operating and expansion sections, distinguishing an unfitted bore from an unexcavated section before assigning transport capacity. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b104-v14-02","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：定量估算","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「路線里程與端點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：長度=13.2 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=13.2 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14.52 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: length=13.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=13.2 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14.52 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用營運配置圖與工程分區核對每段可通行狀態。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Reconcile operating diagrams and works sections to identify the usable status of each segment.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：長度=13.2 km；速度=60 km/h。t=60L/v=13.2 min。僅把長度增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為14.52 min。邊界：假想交通旅程，未含加減速、排隊及實際時刻表；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=13.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=13.2 min. Increasing only length by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 14.52 min. Boundary: Hypothetical transport journey excluding acceleration, queues and the real timetable. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「服務邊界與路線代價」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\", which statement holds?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：長度=13.2 km；速度=60 km/h。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: length=13.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=13.2 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：長度=13.2 km；速度=60 km/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: length=13.2 km; speed=60 km/h. t=60L/v=13.2 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b104-v14-03","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「路線里程與端點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alignment chainage and endpoints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用營運配置圖與工程分區核對每段可通行狀態。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Reconcile operating diagrams and works sections to identify the usable status of each segment. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：用營運配置圖與工程分區核對每段可通行狀態。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile operating diagrams and works sections to identify the usable status of each segment. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","failure":"注意干擾：只有洞體未裝軌的段落若算入容量，會虛構列車交會點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Counting an unfitted bore creates fictitious train-passing opportunities. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用營運配置圖與工程分區核對每段可通行狀態。把縱斷面、地形與地質剖面疊合，以端點坐標獨立反算距離，再將主孔與支坑數量分開核對。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Reconcile operating diagrams and works sections to identify the usable status of each segment. Overlay the longitudinal profile, terrain and geology; independently derive distances from endpoint coordinates and reconcile running-bore and gallery quantities separately. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「路線里程與端點」的交付需回答：用營運配置圖與工程分區核對每段可通行狀態。在方案表中凍結起訖點、計量範圍及地質假設，任何改線都要同步更新高程、數量與服務情境，不能只替換總長。","textEn":"For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the alignment chainage and endpoints handover must address the following evidence: Reconcile operating diagrams and works sections to identify the usable status of each segment. Freeze endpoints, measurement scope and ground assumptions in the option register; realignment requires coordinated updates to elevations, quantities and service scenarios rather than replacing one length.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「服務邊界與路線代價」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\"?","options":["用營運配置圖與工程分區核對每段可通行狀態。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Reconcile operating diagrams and works sections to identify the usable status of each segment.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":0,"explanation":"用營運配置圖與工程分區核對每段可通行狀態。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Reconcile operating diagrams and works sections to identify the usable status of each segment. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b104-v14-04","title":"服務邊界與路線代價：失效診斷","titleEn":"Service boundaries and alignment cost: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「路線里程與端點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alignment chainage and endpoints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只有洞體未裝軌的段落若算入容量，會虛構列車交會點。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Counting an unfitted bore creates fictitious train-passing opportunities. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：比較方案必須使用相同起訖點，並分開主孔、引道及服務坑的工程數量；交通時間只是需求的一個指標，不能代替施工可達性或長期維修評估。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Travel time measures one service benefit but cannot replace assessment of construction access, maintenance closures or exposure to uncertain ground.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只有洞體未裝軌的段落若算入容量，會虛構列車交會點。混用全線與單孔長度會同時扭曲工程數量、行程及逃生距離，造成方案比較失去共同基準。","textEn":"Counting an unfitted bore creates fictitious train-passing opportunities. Mixing whole-route and single-bore lengths distorts quantities, journey time and escape distance, destroying the common basis of an option comparison.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「服務邊界與路線代價」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Service boundaries and alignment cost\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只有洞體未裝軌的段落若算入容量，會虛構列車交會點。","單向理論列車數可以直接當作雙向可承諾營運容量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Counting an unfitted bore creates fictitious train-passing opportunities.","One-direction theoretical train count can be promised as two-way operational capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只有洞體未裝軌的段落若算入容量，會虛構列車交會點。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Counting an unfitted bore creates fictitious train-passing opportunities. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b104-v14-05","title":"單線瓶頸與時距容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Single-track bottlenecks and headway capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-04"],"objective":"說明「區段占用時間」如何影響勒奇山基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Section occupation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Lotschberg Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"以勒奇山單線與雙線相接為情境，將對向列車等待和清空時間分開，辨認貨客混行的容量限制。一段單線或共用道岔會把連續鐵路變成受時間窗限制的系統，清空時間與衝突進路和列車行走時間同樣重要。單方向理論容量只提供上界比較；雙向交會、延誤傳播及維修封鎖會改變可實現班次，必須在共同時距圖中檢查。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「區段占用時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"At a single-to-double-track transition, separate opposing-train waiting from clearance time and identify the constraints imposed by mixed passenger and freight traffic. A single-track section or shared turnout creates time-window constraints, making clearance and conflicting routes as important as travel time. One-direction theoretical capacity gives only a comparison bound. Opposing movements, propagated delays and maintenance closures alter achievable service and must be examined together on a common timetable diagram. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Section occupation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：區段占用=15 min；清空餘裕=2 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: occupation=15 min; clearance=2 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「單向理論列車數可以直接當作雙向可承諾營運容量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One-direction theoretical train count can be promised as two-way operational capacity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「區段占用時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Section occupation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-05-k1","title":"單線瓶頸與時距容量","titleEn":"Single-track bottlenecks and headway capacity","text":"以勒奇山單線與雙線相接為情境，將對向列車等待和清空時間分開，辨認貨客混行的容量限制。一段單線或共用道岔會把連續鐵路變成受時間窗限制的系統，清空時間與衝突進路和列車行走時間同樣重要。","textEn":"At a single-to-double-track transition, separate opposing-train waiting from clearance time and identify the constraints imposed by mixed passenger and freight traffic. A single-track section or shared turnout creates time-window constraints, making clearance and conflicting routes as important as travel time.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：單向理論列車數可以直接當作雙向可承諾營運容量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One-direction theoretical train count can be promised as two-way operational capacity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「單線瓶頸與時距容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Single-track bottlenecks and headway capacity\" is correct?","options":["單向理論列車數可以直接當作雙向可承諾營運容量。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","以勒奇山單線與雙線相接為情境，將對向列車等待和清空時間分開，辨認貨客混行的容量限制。"],"optionsEn":["One-direction theoretical train count can be promised as two-way operational capacity.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","At a single-to-double-track transition, separate opposing-train waiting from clearance time and identify the constraints imposed by mixed passenger and freight traffic."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以勒奇山單線與雙線相接為情境，將對向列車等待和清空時間分開，辨認貨客混行的容量限制。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"At a single-to-double-track transition, separate opposing-train waiting from clearance time and identify the constraints imposed by mixed passenger and freight traffic. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b104-v14-06","title":"單線瓶頸與時距容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Single-track bottlenecks and headway capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「區段占用時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Section occupation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：區段占用=15 min；清空餘裕=2 min。C=60/(tocc+tclear)=3.52941 trains/h。僅把區段占用增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為3.24324 trains/h。邊界：單方向理論容量，未含對向衝突、延誤或維修；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: occupation=15 min; clearance=2 min. C=60/(tocc+tclear)=3.52941 trains/h. Increasing only occupation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 3.24324 trains/h. Boundary: One-direction theoretical capacity without opposing conflicts, delay or maintenance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：重播一個尖峰時段的占用紀錄，加入一列晚到貨車。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Replay one peak-period occupancy record with a delayed freight train added.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：區段占用=15 min；清空餘裕=2 min。C=60/(tocc+tclear)=3.52941 trains/h。僅把區段占用增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為3.24324 trains/h。邊界：單方向理論容量，未含對向衝突、延誤或維修；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: occupation=15 min; clearance=2 min. C=60/(tocc+tclear)=3.52941 trains/h. Increasing only occupation by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 3.24324 trains/h. Boundary: One-direction theoretical capacity without opposing conflicts, delay or maintenance. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「單線瓶頸與時距容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Single-track bottlenecks and headway capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：區段占用=15 min；清空餘裕=2 min。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: occupation=15 min; clearance=2 min.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：區段占用=15 min；清空餘裕=2 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: occupation=15 min; clearance=2 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b104-v14-07","title":"單線瓶頸與時距容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Single-track bottlenecks and headway capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「區段占用時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Section occupation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"重播一個尖峰時段的占用紀錄，加入一列晚到貨車。從列車通過與路線釋放時間戳重建占用，對照進路衝突表，再測試一班延誤如何影響後續交會而非只看平均準點。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Replay one peak-period occupancy record with a delayed freight train added. Reconstruct occupation from passage and release timestamps, compare the route-conflict table and test how one delay affects subsequent meets. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「區段占用時間」的交付需回答：重播一個尖峰時段的占用紀錄，加入一列晚到貨車。容量報告附衝突進路、列車性能和維修窗，任何新增班次須由營運方用可重播的時距圖驗證，不只比較單一每小時數字。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the section occupation time handover must address the following evidence: Replay one peak-period occupancy record with a delayed freight train added. Capacity reports include conflicting routes, train performance and maintenance windows; operations validates additions with replayable timetables rather than one hourly figure.","failure":"注意干擾：只算單向班距會漏掉對向衝突，使時刻表名目容量無法實現。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: One-direction headways omit opposing conflicts and overstate timetable capacity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"重播一個尖峰時段的占用紀錄，加入一列晚到貨車。從列車通過與路線釋放時間戳重建占用，對照進路衝突表，再測試一班延誤如何影響後續交會而非只看平均準點。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Replay one peak-period occupancy record with a delayed freight train added. Reconstruct occupation from passage and release timestamps, compare the route-conflict table and test how one delay affects subsequent meets. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「區段占用時間」的交付需回答：重播一個尖峰時段的占用紀錄，加入一列晚到貨車。容量報告附衝突進路、列車性能和維修窗，任何新增班次須由營運方用可重播的時距圖驗證，不只比較單一每小時數字。","textEn":"For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the section occupation time handover must address the following evidence: Replay one peak-period occupancy record with a delayed freight train added. Capacity reports include conflicting routes, train performance and maintenance windows; operations validates additions with replayable timetables rather than one hourly figure.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「單線瓶頸與時距容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Single-track bottlenecks and headway capacity\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","重播一個尖峰時段的占用紀錄，加入一列晚到貨車。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Replay one peak-period occupancy record with a delayed freight train added.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time."],"answer":1,"explanation":"重播一個尖峰時段的占用紀錄，加入一列晚到貨車。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Replay one peak-period occupancy record with a delayed freight train added. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b104-v14-08","title":"單線瓶頸與時距容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Single-track bottlenecks and headway capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「區段占用時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Section occupation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只算單向班距會漏掉對向衝突，使時刻表名目容量無法實現。把清空時間省略或把雙向列車當同方向排列會高估容量，實際服務可能需要長時間等待才能保留安全間隔。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"One-direction headways omit opposing conflicts and overstate timetable capacity. Omitting clearance or treating opposing trains as one-direction traffic overstates capacity and requires long real waits to preserve separation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：單方向理論容量只提供上界比較；雙向交會、延誤傳播及維修封鎖會改變可實現班次，必須在共同時距圖中檢查。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Opposing movements, propagated delays and maintenance closures alter achievable service and must be examined together on a common timetable diagram.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「單向理論列車數可以直接當作雙向可承諾營運容量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One-direction theoretical train count can be promised as two-way operational capacity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只算單向班距會漏掉對向衝突，使時刻表名目容量無法實現。把清空時間省略或把雙向列車當同方向排列會高估容量，實際服務可能需要長時間等待才能保留安全間隔。","textEn":"One-direction headways omit opposing conflicts and overstate timetable capacity. Omitting clearance or treating opposing trains as one-direction traffic overstates capacity and requires long real waits to preserve separation.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「單線瓶頸與時距容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Single-track bottlenecks and headway capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","只算單向班距會漏掉對向衝突，使時刻表名目容量無法實現。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","One-direction headways omit opposing conflicts and overstate timetable capacity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只算單向班距會漏掉對向衝突，使時刻表名目容量無法實現。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"One-direction headways omit opposing conflicts and overstate timetable capacity. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b104-v14-s2","title":"機制、材料與定量設計","titleEn":"Mechanisms, materials and quantitative design","description":"本階段聚焦「基線縱坡與牽引需求」與「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" and \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b104-v14-09","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-08"],"objective":"說明「坡度阻力功率」如何影響勒奇山基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Grade-resistance power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Lotschberg Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"比較基線路線的低坡度與列車質量，將坡度功率和站外加速需求分開，避免把省能全歸於隧道長度。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「坡度阻力功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Compare low-gradient alignment and train mass, separating grade power from approach acceleration rather than attributing all energy benefit to tunnel length. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain. Civil geometry and power capacity must use consistent train and speed cases. Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grade-resistance power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.26e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0054 無因次；速度=20 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.26e+06 kg; grade=0.0054 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「坡度阻力功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grade-resistance power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-09-k1","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand","text":"比較基線路線的低坡度與列車質量，將坡度功率和站外加速需求分開，避免把省能全歸於隧道長度。基線鐵路用較小縱坡降低重載列車的重力阻力，但仍有滾動、空氣阻力及加速需求。","textEn":"Compare low-gradient alignment and train mass, separating grade power from approach acceleration rather than attributing all energy benefit to tunnel length. A base alignment reduces heavy-train gravity resistance through gentler gradients, but rolling resistance, aerodynamic drag and acceleration remain.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" is correct?","options":["比較基線路線的低坡度與列車質量，將坡度功率和站外加速需求分開，避免把省能全歸於隧道長度。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Compare low-gradient alignment and train mass, separating grade power from approach acceleration rather than attributing all energy benefit to tunnel length.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"比較基線路線的低坡度與列車質量，將坡度功率和站外加速需求分開，避免把省能全歸於隧道長度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Compare low-gradient alignment and train mass, separating grade power from approach acceleration rather than attributing all energy benefit to tunnel length. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b104-v14-10","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：定量估算","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「坡度阻力功率」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Grade-resistance power” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：列車質量=1.26e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0054 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1334.94 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1468.44 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.26e+06 kg; grade=0.0054 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1334.94 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1468.44 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：核對縱斷面坡度符號、列車質量和同速區段的功率。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Check gradient sign, train mass and power over equal-speed sections.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.26e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0054 無因次；速度=20 m/s。P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1334.94 kW。僅把縱坡增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為1468.44 kW。邊界：僅坡度阻力，不含滾動、氣動、加速及效率；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.26e+06 kg; grade=0.0054 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. P=mgiv/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=1334.94 kW. Increasing only grade by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 1468.44 kW. Boundary: Grade resistance only, excluding rolling, aerodynamic, acceleration and efficiency losses. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「基線縱坡與牽引需求」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\", which statement holds?","options":["增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","原創教學假設：列車質量=1.26e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0054 無因次；速度=20 m/s。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.26e+06 kg; grade=0.0054 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：列車質量=1.26e+06 kg；縱坡=0.0054 無因次；速度=20 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: train mass=1.26e+06 kg; grade=0.0054 dimensionless; speed=20 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b104-v14-11","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「坡度阻力功率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Grade-resistance power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"核對縱斷面坡度符號、列車質量和同速區段的功率。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Check gradient sign, train mass and power over equal-speed sections. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：核對縱斷面坡度符號、列車質量和同速區段的功率。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Check gradient sign, train mass and power over equal-speed sections. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","failure":"注意干擾：下坡回生未計效率時可能被當作全部可回收能量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Ignoring regenerative efficiency can overstate recoverable downhill energy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"核對縱斷面坡度符號、列車質量和同速區段的功率。以里程高程表逐段計算坡度，對照列車性能曲線和供電模型，另檢核低速牽引及下坡制動，不只比較平均功率。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Check gradient sign, train mass and power over equal-speed sections. Calculate local grades from chainage and elevation, compare with train-performance and power models, and separately check low-speed traction and downhill braking. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「坡度阻力功率」的交付需回答：核對縱斷面坡度符號、列車質量和同速區段的功率。軌頂高程交付前，由土建、軌道、供電和營運共同確認同版線形及列車包絡，變更坡度時同步更新性能與容量計算。","textEn":"For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the grade-resistance power handover must address the following evidence: Check gradient sign, train mass and power over equal-speed sections. Civil, track, power and operations teams approve one alignment and train envelope before handover; grade changes update both performance and capacity calculations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「基線縱坡與牽引需求」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","核對縱斷面坡度符號、列車質量和同速區段的功率。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Check gradient sign, train mass and power over equal-speed sections."],"answer":2,"explanation":"核對縱斷面坡度符號、列車質量和同速區段的功率。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Check gradient sign, train mass and power over equal-speed sections. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b104-v14-12","title":"基線縱坡與牽引需求：失效診斷","titleEn":"Base-alignment grade and traction demand: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「坡度阻力功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Grade-resistance power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"下坡回生未計效率時可能被當作全部可回收能量。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Ignoring regenerative efficiency can overstate recoverable downhill energy. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：土建線形和供電容量必須使用同一列車與速度情境，短距陡坡也不能被平均坡度掩蓋；制動方向的能量處理則是另一個需要獨立檢核的工況。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Short steep sections cannot be hidden in an average gradient, while braking energy in the opposite direction requires its own operating and electrical assessment.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"下坡回生未計效率時可能被當作全部可回收能量。平均坡度低卻存在短陡坡時，峰值功率可能超過預估，速度下降又會增加區段占用時間，牽連營運容量。","textEn":"Ignoring regenerative efficiency can overstate recoverable downhill energy. A short steep grade can exceed power estimates despite a low average, reducing speed and extending block occupation with capacity consequences.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「基線縱坡與牽引需求」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Base-alignment grade and traction demand\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["下坡回生未計效率時可能被當作全部可回收能量。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Ignoring regenerative efficiency can overstate recoverable downhill energy.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"下坡回生未計效率時可能被當作全部可回收能量。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Ignoring regenerative efficiency can overstate recoverable downhill energy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b104-v14-13","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-12"],"objective":"說明「測壓水頭」如何影響勒奇山基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Piezometric head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Lotschberg Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"勒奇山擴建的教學模型保留營運孔排水與新開挖孔之間的水力連通，檢查新排水是否改變既有孔外壓。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「測壓水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Retain hydraulic connectivity between the operating bore and a hypothetical new heading, testing whether new drainage changes pressure around the existing bore. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level. Drainage reduces pressure but can increase effective stress and settlement. Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piezometric head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=45 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=45 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=441.45 kPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「測壓水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piezometric head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-13-k1","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure","text":"勒奇山擴建的教學模型保留營運孔排水與新開挖孔之間的水力連通，檢查新排水是否改變既有孔外壓。水壓取決於連通含水層的測壓水頭，不必等於地表或海面至洞頂的幾何深度。","textEn":"Retain hydraulic connectivity between the operating bore and a hypothetical new heading, testing whether new drainage changes pressure around the existing bore. Water pressure follows piezometric head in the connected aquifer, not automatically the geometric depth below ground or sea level.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" is correct?","options":["目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。","勒奇山擴建的教學模型保留營運孔排水與新開挖孔之間的水力連通，檢查新排水是否改變既有孔外壓。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.","Retain hydraulic connectivity between the operating bore and a hypothetical new heading, testing whether new drainage changes pressure around the existing bore.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"勒奇山擴建的教學模型保留營運孔排水與新開挖孔之間的水力連通，檢查新排水是否改變既有孔外壓。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Retain hydraulic connectivity between the operating bore and a hypothetical new heading, testing whether new drainage changes pressure around the existing bore. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b104-v14-14","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「測壓水頭」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Piezometric head” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=45 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=441.45 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為485.595 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=45 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=441.45 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 485.595 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：配對兩孔水頭與出流歷線，標示新孔施工事件。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair both-bore heads and flows against new-heading construction events.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=45 m。p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=441.45 kPa。僅把水頭增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為485.595 kPa。邊界：靜水表壓，不是土體總壓或原位量測；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=45 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=441.45 kPa. Increasing only head by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 485.595 kPa. Boundary: Hydrostatic gauge pressure, not total earth pressure or an in-situ measurement. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\", which statement holds?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=45 m。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=45 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=441.45 kPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：水密度=1000 kg/m³；水頭=45 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: water density=1000 kg/m³; head=45 m. p=ρgh/1000, g=9.81 m/s²=441.45 kPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b104-v14-15","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「測壓水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Piezometric head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"配對兩孔水頭與出流歷線，標示新孔施工事件。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair both-bore heads and flows against new-heading construction events. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：配對兩孔水頭與出流歷線，標示新孔施工事件。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Pair both-bore heads and flows against new-heading construction events. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","failure":"注意干擾：共同水頭下降不應被誤判為兩套排水設備同時改善。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shared drawdown should not be mistaken for independent improvement of both drainage systems. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"配對兩孔水頭與出流歷線，標示新孔施工事件。使用分層測壓管及流量計，配合降雨或潮位序列分辨補注與設備影響，將讀值統一換算至同一高程基準。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Pair both-bore heads and flows against new-heading construction events. Use nested piezometers and flowmeters with rainfall or tide histories to distinguish recharge from equipment effects, converting observations to a common elevation datum. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「測壓水頭」的交付需回答：配對兩孔水頭與出流歷線，標示新孔施工事件。設計檢核應分列正常排水、堵塞與停電水位，將環境受體的容許變化和監測責任一起交付，不把抽水量當唯一指標。","textEn":"For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the piezometric head handover must address the following evidence: Pair both-bore heads and flows against new-heading construction events. Separate normal drainage, blocked-drain and power-outage heads and hand over receptor limits and monitoring responsibility together rather than using pump flow as the sole indicator.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\"?","options":["配對兩孔水頭與出流歷線，標示新孔施工事件。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Pair both-bore heads and flows against new-heading construction events.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":0,"explanation":"配對兩孔水頭與出流歷線，標示新孔施工事件。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair both-bore heads and flows against new-heading construction events. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b104-v14-16","title":"測壓水頭與襯砌外壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Piezometric head and lining pressure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「測壓水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Piezometric head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"共同水頭下降不應被誤判為兩套排水設備同時改善。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shared drawdown should not be mistaken for independent improvement of both drainage systems. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：排水降低水壓卻可能增加有效應力與沉陷；停泵或排水堵塞後水頭又會回升，因此防水、排水及環境保水是互相制約的設計選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Head may recover after a pump outage or blockage, coupling waterproofing, drainage capacity and preservation of surrounding groundwater in the permanent design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"共同水頭下降不應被誤判為兩套排水設備同時改善。將暫時降水後的低水頭當成永久狀態，會漏掉停泵後外壓回升；過度排水也可能引起周邊地層壓密。","textEn":"Shared drawdown should not be mistaken for independent improvement of both drainage systems. Treating temporarily lowered head as permanent misses pressure recovery after outage; excessive drainage can also consolidate surrounding ground.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「測壓水頭與襯砌外壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Piezometric head and lining pressure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","共同水頭下降不應被誤判為兩套排水設備同時改善。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Shared drawdown should not be mistaken for independent improvement of both drainage systems.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"共同水頭下降不應被誤判為兩套排水設備同時改善。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shared drawdown should not be mistaken for independent improvement of both drainage systems. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b104-v14-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「支護啟動與變形容量」與「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" and \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b104-v14-17","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-16"],"objective":"說明「支護安裝時點」如何影響勒奇山基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Support activation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Lotschberg Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"在未完成洞段重新進場的情境中，分析舊支護齡期、暴露環境與新開挖釋放的疊加，不直接沿用原施工期參數。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支護安裝時點」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"For re-entry to an unfinished section, examine aged support, exposure and renewed excavation release rather than reusing original construction parameters unchanged. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces. Interpret ground-reaction and support curves together with distance from the face and closure sequence. Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Support activation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：局部剛度=33 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=33 kN/mm; movement=9 mm.","failure":"常見誤解：「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「支護安裝時點」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Support activation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-17-k1","title":"支護啟動與變形容量","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity","text":"在未完成洞段重新進場的情境中，分析舊支護齡期、暴露環境與新開挖釋放的疊加，不直接沿用原施工期參數。支護荷載由開挖釋放量和支護啟動時間共同決定，越早安裝不一定讓構件受力越小。","textEn":"For re-entry to an unfinished section, examine aged support, exposure and renewed excavation release rather than reusing original construction parameters unchanged. Support load depends on stress release and activation time, so earlier installation does not necessarily reduce member forces.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" is correct?","options":["支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","在未完成洞段重新進場的情境中，分析舊支護齡期、暴露環境與新開挖釋放的疊加，不直接沿用原施工期參數。"],"optionsEn":["Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","For re-entry to an unfinished section, examine aged support, exposure and renewed excavation release rather than reusing original construction parameters unchanged."],"answer":2,"explanation":"在未完成洞段重新進場的情境中，分析舊支護齡期、暴露環境與新開挖釋放的疊加，不直接沿用原施工期參數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"For re-entry to an unfinished section, examine aged support, exposure and renewed excavation release rather than reusing original construction parameters unchanged. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b104-v14-18","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：定量估算","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支護安裝時點」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Support activation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：局部剛度=33 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。F=ku=297 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為326.7 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=33 kN/mm; movement=9 mm. F=ku=297 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 326.7 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將舊裂縫圖與新收斂基線配對，區分既有和新增變形。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Pair legacy crack maps with a new convergence baseline to distinguish old and new movement.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=33 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。F=ku=297 kN。僅把位移增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為326.7 kN。邊界：線性局部彈簧，不含屈服或時間效應；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=33 kN/mm; movement=9 mm. F=ku=297 kN. Increasing only movement by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 326.7 kN. Boundary: Local linear spring without yielding or time effects. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支護啟動與變形容量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Support activation and deformation capacity\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：局部剛度=33 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=33 kN/mm; movement=9 mm.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：局部剛度=33 kN/mm；位移=9 mm。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: local stiffness=33 kN/mm; movement=9 mm. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b104-v14-19","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支護安裝時點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Support activation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將舊裂縫圖與新收斂基線配對，區分既有和新增變形。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Pair legacy crack maps with a new convergence baseline to distinguish old and new movement. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：將舊裂縫圖與新收斂基線配對，區分既有和新增變形。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Pair legacy crack maps with a new convergence baseline to distinguish old and new movement. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","failure":"注意干擾：把舊裂縫全部視為新施工所致會誤導支護判讀。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Attributing all old cracks to new works misdirects support interpretation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將舊裂縫圖與新收斂基線配對，區分既有和新增變形。同步記錄收斂、支護荷重與安裝里程，比較同一地質分區內的速率及荷載，不將不同開挖齡期讀值直接混合。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Pair legacy crack maps with a new convergence baseline to distinguish old and new movement. Synchronise convergence, support loads and installation chainage; compare rates and loads within one ground domain without mixing readings at different excavation ages. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「支護安裝時點」的交付需回答：將舊裂縫圖與新收斂基線配對，區分既有和新增變形。把安裝時間和量測資料一起交付支護設計者，任何級別變更都需地質及位移證據，不能憑單一瞬間讀值自行改支護。","textEn":"For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the support activation time handover must address the following evidence: Pair legacy crack maps with a new convergence baseline to distinguish old and new movement. Submit installation times with measurements to the support designer; class changes need both ground and movement evidence, not an isolated instantaneous reading.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支護啟動與變形容量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Support activation and deformation capacity\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","將舊裂縫圖與新收斂基線配對，區分既有和新增變形。","單向理論列車數可以直接當作雙向可承諾營運容量。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Pair legacy crack maps with a new convergence baseline to distinguish old and new movement.","One-direction theoretical train count can be promised as two-way operational capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"將舊裂縫圖與新收斂基線配對，區分既有和新增變形。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Pair legacy crack maps with a new convergence baseline to distinguish old and new movement. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b104-v14-20","title":"支護啟動與變形容量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Support activation and deformation capacity: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支護安裝時點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Support activation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把舊裂縫全部視為新施工所致會誤導支護判讀。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Attributing all old cracks to new works misdirects support interpretation. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：地盤反力與支護曲線必須連同掌子面距離及封閉順序理解；擠壓性地層還需保留變形容量，不能只追求高剛度與高材料強度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Squeezing ground also needs deformation capacity; high stiffness and material strength alone do not guarantee a compatible support response.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把舊裂縫全部視為新施工所致會誤導支護判讀。過晚封閉會讓不可回復變形增加，過硬且行程不足的支護也可能脆裂，兩者都可能表現為裂縫而需不同處理。","textEn":"Attributing all old cracks to new works misdirects support interpretation. Late closure increases irreversible movement, while excessively stiff support with little travel can fail brittly; both produce cracks but require different diagnoses.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支護啟動與變形容量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Support activation and deformation capacity\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","把舊裂縫全部視為新施工所致會誤導支護判讀。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Attributing all old cracks to new works misdirects support interpretation."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把舊裂縫全部視為新施工所致會誤導支護判讀。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Attributing all old cracks to new works misdirects support interpretation. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b104-v14-21","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-20"],"objective":"說明「出渣運輸節拍」如何影響勒奇山基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Muck-transport cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Lotschberg Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"營運旁擴建需要共用入口時，列車、材料與維修人員各自占用時間，不能假設夜間窗口全供出渣。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出渣運輸節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When expansion shares access with operations, trains, materials and maintainers each occupy time; a night window is not entirely available for spoil transport. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together. Shared shafts or railways become serial bottlenecks, while queues and maintenance reduce nominal capacity. Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Muck-transport cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=23 t；往返週期=35 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=23 t; cycle=35 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「出渣運輸節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Muck-transport cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-21-k1","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks","text":"營運旁擴建需要共用入口時，列車、材料與維修人員各自占用時間，不能假設夜間窗口全供出渣。多工作面只有在供電、通風、出渣與材料供應同步充足時才增加總產量。","textEn":"When expansion shares access with operations, trains, materials and maintainers each occupy time; a night window is not entirely available for spoil transport. Multiple headings increase output only when power, air, muck transport and materials support them together.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" is correct?","options":["營運旁擴建需要共用入口時，列車、材料與維修人員各自占用時間，不能假設夜間窗口全供出渣。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["When expansion shares access with operations, trains, materials and maintainers each occupy time; a night window is not entirely available for spoil transport.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"營運旁擴建需要共用入口時，列車、材料與維修人員各自占用時間，不能假設夜間窗口全供出渣。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When expansion shares access with operations, trains, materials and maintainers each occupy time; a night window is not entirely available for spoil transport. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b104-v14-22","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：定量估算","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「出渣運輸節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Muck-transport cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=23 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=157.714 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為143.377 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=23 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=157.714 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 143.377 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：將保護設置和恢復營運時間從窗口中明確扣除。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Explicitly deduct protection setup and restoration time from each access window.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=23 t；往返週期=35 min。C=N payload 60/T=157.714 t/h。僅把往返週期增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為143.377 t/h。邊界：無排隊理想循環，並非共享路段實際產能；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=23 t; cycle=35 min. C=N payload 60/T=157.714 t/h. Increasing only cycle by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 143.377 t/h. Boundary: Ideal cycle without queues, not actual shared-route production. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\", which statement holds?","options":["只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=23 t；往返週期=35 min。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=23 t; cycle=35 min.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：車輛數=4 個；每車載量=23 t；往返週期=35 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: vehicles=4 count; payload=23 t; cycle=35 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b104-v14-23","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「出渣運輸節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Muck-transport cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"將保護設置和恢復營運時間從窗口中明確扣除。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Explicitly deduct protection setup and restoration time from each access window. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：將保護設置和恢復營運時間從窗口中明確扣除。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Explicitly deduct protection setup and restoration time from each access window. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","failure":"注意干擾：忽略恢復檢查會使最後一車出渣與首班營運列車衝突。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted restoration checks create conflict between the final spoil movement and first service. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"將保護設置和恢復營運時間從窗口中明確扣除。以裝載質量、往返時間及排隊時間重建物流曲線，再核對緩衝占用、共用通道優先權與維修時段。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Explicitly deduct protection setup and restoration time from each access window. Reconstruct flow from payload, round-trip and queue times, then check buffer occupancy, shared-route priorities and maintenance periods. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「出渣運輸節拍」的交付需回答：將保護設置和恢復營運時間從窗口中明確扣除。每日排程同時標示人員、材料和維修的占用時段，任何物流改線先檢查通風與應變通道，不能只看運量提升。","textEn":"For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the muck-transport cycle handover must address the following evidence: Explicitly deduct protection setup and restoration time from each access window. Schedules show personnel, materials and maintenance occupancy together; rerouting first checks ventilation and emergency access rather than only throughput gains.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","將保護設置和恢復營運時間從窗口中明確扣除。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Explicitly deduct protection setup and restoration time from each access window."],"answer":2,"explanation":"將保護設置和恢復營運時間從窗口中明確扣除。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Explicitly deduct protection setup and restoration time from each access window. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b104-v14-24","title":"共享通道與運輸瓶頸：失效診斷","titleEn":"Shared access and transport bottlenecks: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「出渣運輸節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Muck-transport cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"忽略恢復檢查會使最後一車出渣與首班營運列車衝突。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted restoration checks create conflict between the final spoil movement and first service. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：共用豎井或軌道形成串聯瓶頸，排隊和維修窗口會降低名目容量；緩衝區太大又可能侵占通行與救援空間，因此不能單純把各面產能相加。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Large buffers may obstruct personnel and rescue access, so face capacities cannot simply be added without a network-level transport and storage check.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"忽略恢復檢查會使最後一車出渣與首班營運列車衝突。把理想往返時間當全天常數會忽略交會等待與卸料堵塞，導致工作面停工或把材料堆入必要通道。","textEn":"Omitted restoration checks create conflict between the final spoil movement and first service. Treating an ideal cycle as constant all day misses passing delays and unloading blockages, stopping headings or pushing material into essential access space.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「共享通道與運輸瓶頸」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Shared access and transport bottlenecks\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["忽略恢復檢查會使最後一車出渣與首班營運列車衝突。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Omitted restoration checks create conflict between the final spoil movement and first service.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"忽略恢復檢查會使最後一車出渣與首班營運列車衝突。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted restoration checks create conflict between the final spoil movement and first service. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b104-v14-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「控制網與貫通誤差」與「通風網路與壓力損失」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Control network and breakthrough error\" and \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b104-v14-25","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-24"],"objective":"說明「方向角誤差」如何影響勒奇山基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Orientation error” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Lotschberg Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"擴建需接回既有軌道控制網，研究新舊坐標、溫度和軌道維修基準不一致所造成的累積偏差。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向角誤差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Expansion must reconnect with existing track control, so examine bias from differing coordinate revisions, temperatures and maintenance reference systems. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control. A small closure does not exclude systematic bias: scale, refraction, orientation and vertical datum may shift together. Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Orientation error” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：控制長度=3360 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3360 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0423533 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「方向角誤差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Orientation error”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-25-k1","title":"控制網與貫通誤差","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error","text":"擴建需接回既有軌道控制網，研究新舊坐標、溫度和軌道維修基準不一致所造成的累積偏差。長隧道的微小方向誤差會沿距離累積，地下控制網又缺少直接衛星定位，必須把地表基準可靠傳到洞內。","textEn":"Expansion must reconnect with existing track control, so examine bias from differing coordinate revisions, temperatures and maintenance reference systems. Small orientation errors accumulate over long drives, while underground networks lack direct satellite positioning and depend on transferring surface control.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Control network and breakthrough error\" is correct?","options":["兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。","擴建需接回既有軌道控制網，研究新舊坐標、溫度和軌道維修基準不一致所造成的累積偏差。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.","Expansion must reconnect with existing track control, so examine bias from differing coordinate revisions, temperatures and maintenance reference systems.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"擴建需接回既有軌道控制網，研究新舊坐標、溫度和軌道維修基準不一致所造成的累積偏差。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Expansion must reconnect with existing track control, so examine bias from differing coordinate revisions, temperatures and maintenance reference systems. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b104-v14-26","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：定量估算","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「方向角誤差」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Orientation error” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：控制長度=3360 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0423533 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0465887 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: control length=3360 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0423533 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0465887 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以獨立控制線核對新舊網的尺度及高程轉換。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Independently verify scale and height transformations between old and new networks.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3360 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0423533 m。僅把方向偏角增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為0.0465887 m。邊界：小角度方向偏差，未加入控制網相關性及折光；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3360 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0423533 m. Increasing only orientation error by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 0.0465887 m. Boundary: Small-angle orientation error without network correlation or refraction. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「控制網與貫通誤差」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Control network and breakthrough error\", which statement holds?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","單向理論列車數可以直接當作雙向可承諾營運容量。","原創教學假設：控制長度=3360 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","One-direction theoretical train count can be promised as two-way operational capacity.","Original teaching assumptions: control length=3360 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0423533 m."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：控制長度=3360 m；方向偏角=2.6 arcsec。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: control length=3360 m; orientation error=2.6 arcsec. e=Lθπ/(180×3600)=0.0423533 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b104-v14-27","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「方向角誤差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Orientation error” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以獨立控制線核對新舊網的尺度及高程轉換。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Independently verify scale and height transformations between old and new networks. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：以獨立控制線核對新舊網的尺度及高程轉換。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently verify scale and height transformations between old and new networks. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","failure":"注意干擾：只比坐標數字而未比版本可能把基準移動當結構位移。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Comparing coordinates without revisions confuses datum change with structural movement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以獨立控制線核對新舊網的尺度及高程轉換。由獨立測量組複核地表到洞內的轉換，保留原始角距及溫度資料，用不同控制線比較方向與高程偏差。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Independently verify scale and height transformations between old and new networks. Independently check surface-to-tunnel transformations, retain raw angles, distances and temperatures, and compare orientation and elevation through separate control routes. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「方向角誤差」的交付需回答：以獨立控制線核對新舊網的尺度及高程轉換。貫通前凍結座標、尺度與高程版本，獨立組直接使用原始觀測重算；不得只傳遞整理好的坐標而遺失校正資訊。","textEn":"For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the orientation error handover must address the following evidence: Independently verify scale and height transformations between old and new networks. Freeze coordinate, scale and height revisions before breakthrough; independent reviewers recompute raw observations rather than receiving only adjusted coordinates without corrections.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「控制網與貫通誤差」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Control network and breakthrough error\"?","options":["以獨立控制線核對新舊網的尺度及高程轉換。","量測時不必記錄溫度、水頭、開挖序列與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["Independently verify scale and height transformations between old and new networks.","Temperature, water head, excavation sequence and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以獨立控制線核對新舊網的尺度及高程轉換。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Independently verify scale and height transformations between old and new networks. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b104-v14-28","title":"控制網與貫通誤差：失效診斷","titleEn":"Control network and breakthrough error: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「方向角誤差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Orientation error” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只比坐標數字而未比版本可能把基準移動當結構位移。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Comparing coordinates without revisions confuses datum change with structural movement. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：閉合差很小不代表無系統誤差；尺度、折光、儀器定向與高程基準可能共同偏移，誤差相關性也使平方和估算失真。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Correlated errors also invalidate a naive root-sum-square combination of supposedly independent observations.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只比坐標數字而未比版本可能把基準移動當結構位移。共用錯誤基準可能讓兩組測量同時看似一致，直到貫通或軌道銜接才發現系統偏差，修正成本遠高於早期複核。","textEn":"Comparing coordinates without revisions confuses datum change with structural movement. A shared wrong datum can make separate surveys appear consistent until breakthrough or track connection exposes bias that is costly to correct.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「控制網與貫通誤差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Control network and breakthrough error\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","只比坐標數字而未比版本可能把基準移動當結構位移。","風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Comparing coordinates without revisions confuses datum change with structural movement.","Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只比坐標數字而未比版本可能把基準移動當結構位移。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Comparing coordinates without revisions confuses datum change with structural movement. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b104-v14-29","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-28"],"objective":"說明「風道摩擦壓損」如何影響勒奇山基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Duct friction loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Lotschberg Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"以施工區與營運區隔離為題，分析門位及施工風管改變時兩區壓差，保留營運事故模式的獨立需求。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風道摩擦壓損」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Study pressure differences across construction-operational isolation as doors and temporary ducts change, retaining the separate requirements of operational incident modes. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans. Switching a branch redistributes the network rather than simply adding rated flows. Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Duct friction loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=620 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=620 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=31.8292 Pa.","failure":"常見誤解：「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「風道摩擦壓損」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Duct friction loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-29-k1","title":"通風網路與壓力損失","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss","text":"以施工區與營運區隔離為題，分析門位及施工風管改變時兩區壓差，保留營運事故模式的獨立需求。風機提供壓差，實際風量由風道摩阻、局部損失、外風與其他風機共同決定。","textEn":"Study pressure differences across construction-operational isolation as doors and temporary ducts change, retaining the separate requirements of operational incident modes. Fans supply pressure, but actual flow follows friction, local losses, external wind and interactions with other fans.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" is correct?","options":["風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","以施工區與營運區隔離為題，分析門位及施工風管改變時兩區壓差，保留營運事故模式的獨立需求。"],"optionsEn":["Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Study pressure differences across construction-operational isolation as doors and temporary ducts change, retaining the separate requirements of operational incident modes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以施工區與營運區隔離為題，分析門位及施工風管改變時兩區壓差，保留營運事故模式的獨立需求。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Study pressure differences across construction-operational isolation as doors and temporary ducts change, retaining the separate requirements of operational incident modes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b104-v14-30","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：定量估算","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「風道摩擦壓損」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Duct friction loss” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=620 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=31.8292 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為38.5134 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=620 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=31.8292 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 38.5134 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在核准隔離狀態下比對施工側風量與營運側壓差。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Compare construction airflow and operational pressure under approved isolation states.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=620 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=31.8292 Pa。僅把平均風速增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為38.5134 Pa。邊界：定密度直管摩阻，局部損失及外風另計；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=620 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=31.8292 Pa. Increasing only mean velocity by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 38.5134 Pa. Boundary: Constant-density straight-duct friction; local loss and external wind are separate. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「通風網路與壓力損失」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\", which statement holds?","options":["原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=620 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。","基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。"],"optionsEn":["Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk.","A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創教學假設：達西因子=0.025 無因次；風道長度=620 m；水力直徑=4 m；空氣密度=1.2 kg/m³；平均風速=3.7 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: Darcy factor=0.025 dimensionless; duct length=620 m; hydraulic diameter=4 m; air density=1.2 kg/m³; mean velocity=3.7 m/s. Δp=f(L/D)ρv²/2=31.8292 Pa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b104-v14-31","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「風道摩擦壓損」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Duct friction loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在核准隔離狀態下比對施工側風量與營運側壓差。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Compare construction airflow and operational pressure under approved isolation states. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：在核准隔離狀態下比對施工側風量與營運側壓差。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare construction airflow and operational pressure under approved isolation states. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","failure":"注意干擾：施工排風若短路到營運區，兩側感測器可能各自顯示正常局部風速。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A construction-air shortcut may coexist with apparently normal local velocities on both sides. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在核准隔離狀態下比對施工側風量與營運側壓差。沿線同步量測靜壓與風速，記錄風門及其他風機狀態，再把實測工作點和風機曲線、網路壓損比較。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Compare construction airflow and operational pressure under approved isolation states. Measure pressure and velocity synchronously, record dampers and other fans, and compare the measured duty point with fan curves and network resistance. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「風道摩擦壓損」的交付需回答：在核准隔離狀態下比對施工側風量與營運側壓差。驗收採明確風門和車流邊界，維修改線後重新核對網路工作點，火災模式由防災責任工程師簽認而非沿用正常模式。","textEn":"For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the duct friction loss handover must address the following evidence: Compare construction airflow and operational pressure under approved isolation states. Commission with specified damper and traffic boundaries, recheck duty points after rerouting, and have the fire-safety engineer approve emergency modes independently.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「通風網路與壓力損失」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\"?","options":["沿用另一條隧道或另一處地層的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在核准隔離狀態下比對施工側風量與營運側壓差。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another tunnel or ground formation counts as verifying this structure.","Compare construction airflow and operational pressure under approved isolation states.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在核准隔離狀態下比對施工側風量與營運側壓差。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Compare construction airflow and operational pressure under approved isolation states. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b104-v14-32","title":"通風網路與壓力損失：失效診斷","titleEn":"Ventilation network and pressure loss: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「風道摩擦壓損」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Duct friction loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"施工排風若短路到營運區，兩側感測器可能各自顯示正常局部風速。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A construction-air shortcut may coexist with apparently normal local velocities on both sides. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：支路開關會重新分配整個網路，不能把額定風量直接加總；正常污染稀釋與火災控煙也有不同目標，需要分別建立受控邊界和故障情境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Routine dilution and fire smoke control have different objectives, so each needs explicit boundaries, operating states and failure cases rather than one universal flow target.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「風機銘牌風量相加就是全隧道各處可用的通風量。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adding fan nameplate flows gives the usable airflow everywhere in the tunnel.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"施工排風若短路到營運區，兩側感測器可能各自顯示正常局部風速。只看風機轉速會漏掉風門誤位或短路漏風，可能在總耗電增加時，真正需要的區段反而風量不足。","textEn":"A construction-air shortcut may coexist with apparently normal local velocities on both sides. Fan speed alone misses a misplaced damper or leakage shortcut; total power may rise while the critical section receives less air.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「通風網路與壓力損失」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Ventilation network and pressure loss\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","施工排風若短路到營運區，兩側感測器可能各自顯示正常局部風速。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","A construction-air shortcut may coexist with apparently normal local velocities on both sides."],"answer":2,"explanation":"施工排風若短路到營運區，兩側感測器可能各自顯示正常局部風速。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A construction-air shortcut may coexist with apparently normal local velocities on both sides. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b104-v14-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「疏散時間與分區可用性」與「資產編碼與可追溯交接」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" and \"Asset identity and traceable handover\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b104-v14-33","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-32"],"objective":"說明「所需疏散時間」如何影響勒奇山基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Required evacuation time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Lotschberg Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"分期工程的避難路徑可能穿越暫時封閉區域，建立依施工階段變動的路線圖，不能只保留最終完工配置。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「所需疏散時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Staged works can temporarily close an escape route; maintain stage-specific access maps rather than relying only on the final completed arrangement. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit. Smoke, visibility and mobility alter walking speed, while safety requires comparison with available safe time. A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Required evacuation time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：前置時間=86 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=86 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「所需疏散時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Required evacuation time”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-33-k1","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability","text":"分期工程的避難路徑可能穿越暫時封閉區域，建立依施工階段變動的路線圖，不能只保留最終完工配置。疏散時間包含辨識、反應、移動及排隊，不只由出口距離決定。","textEn":"Staged works can temporarily close an escape route; maintain stage-specific access maps rather than relying only on the final completed arrangement. Evacuation includes detection, response, travel and queues, not merely distance to an exit.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" is correct?","options":["分期工程的避難路徑可能穿越暫時封閉區域，建立依施工階段變動的路線圖，不能只保留最終完工配置。","只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["Staged works can temporarily close an escape route; maintain stage-specific access maps rather than relying only on the final completed arrangement.","Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分期工程的避難路徑可能穿越暫時封閉區域，建立依施工階段變動的路線圖，不能只保留最終完工配置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Staged works can temporarily close an escape route; maintain stage-specific access maps rather than relying only on the final completed arrangement. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b104-v14-34","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：定量估算","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「所需疏散時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Required evacuation time” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：前置時間=86 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=536 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為581 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=86 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=536 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 581 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：走查每個施工階段的門位、可通行淨寬和資訊標示。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Walk each stage to check door state, usable width and signs.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：前置時間=86 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。RSET=tpre+d/v=536 s。僅把行走距離增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為581 s。邊界：單群體固定速度，不含排隊煙熱及能力差異，不能單獨判安全；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=86 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. RSET=tpre+d/v=536 s. Increasing only travel distance by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 581 s. Boundary: One group at fixed speed without queues, smoke or mobility differences; not a safety conclusion. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「疏散時間與分區可用性」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Evacuation time and zone availability\", which statement holds?","options":["單向理論列車數可以直接當作雙向可承諾營運容量。","原創教學假設：前置時間=86 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。","目前沒有可見漏水就能在設計中忽略外水壓。"],"optionsEn":["One-direction theoretical train count can be promised as two-way operational capacity.","Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=86 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s.","No visible leakage means that external water pressure can be omitted from design."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創教學假設：前置時間=86 s；行走距離=360 m；行走速度=0.8 m/s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: pre-movement time=86 s; travel distance=360 m; walking speed=0.8 m/s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b104-v14-35","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「所需疏散時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Required evacuation time” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"走查每個施工階段的門位、可通行淨寬和資訊標示。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Walk each stage to check door state, usable width and signs. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：走查每個施工階段的門位、可通行淨寬和資訊標示。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Walk each stage to check door state, usable width and signs. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","failure":"注意干擾：舊版逃生圖若仍指向施工封閉段，距離計算再精確也無效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An obsolete map leading into a closed works zone invalidates precise distance calculations. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"走查每個施工階段的門位、可通行淨寬和資訊標示。以人流模擬或受控演練分辨前置時間、行走與門口排隊，核對每個出口接收區的可用狀態及通訊紀錄。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Walk each stage to check door state, usable width and signs. Separate pre-movement, travel and doorway queues through simulation or controlled drills, checking receiving-zone availability and communication records for each exit. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「所需疏散時間」的交付需回答：走查每個施工階段的門位、可通行淨寬和資訊標示。疏散模型保留人口、速度分布及出口狀態，演練改動由營運與防災責任者批准，教材算例不得當作現場指揮程序。","textEn":"For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the required evacuation time handover must address the following evidence: Walk each stage to check door state, usable width and signs. Retain population, speed distribution and exit states; operations and fire-safety owners approve drill changes, and classroom calculations are not incident-command procedures.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「疏散時間與分區可用性」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Evacuation time and zone availability\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","增加工作面就可以直接把各面的理論產量相加。","走查每個施工階段的門位、可通行淨寬和資訊標示。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","Adding headings allows their theoretical outputs to be summed directly.","Walk each stage to check door state, usable width and signs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"走查每個施工階段的門位、可通行淨寬和資訊標示。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Walk each stage to check door state, usable width and signs. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b104-v14-36","title":"疏散時間與分區可用性：失效診斷","titleEn":"Evacuation time and zone availability: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「所需疏散時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Required evacuation time” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"舊版逃生圖若仍指向施工封閉段，距離計算再精確也無效。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An obsolete map leading into a closed works zone invalidates precise distance calculations. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：人員速度會受煙熱、能見度及行動能力影響，安全判斷還要比較可用安全時間；橫通道存在但門或鄰孔不可用時，圖上的最短路線不一定能作實際選擇。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A passage shown on a plan may be unusable because its door or receiving bore is unavailable, invalidating the nominal shortest route.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要出口距離短，就不需要比較可用與所需安全時間。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Short exit distance removes the need to compare available and required safe time.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"舊版逃生圖若仍指向施工封閉段，距離計算再精確也無效。以最快成人速度套全部旅客會低估需求，若忽略接收孔受煙或車流影響，疏散可能移到另一個危險邊界。","textEn":"An obsolete map leading into a closed works zone invalidates precise distance calculations. Applying the fastest adult speed to everyone understates demand; overlooking smoke or traffic in the receiving bore can transfer evacuees into another hazard.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「疏散時間與分區可用性」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Evacuation time and zone availability\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["舊版逃生圖若仍指向施工封閉段，距離計算再精確也無效。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。"],"optionsEn":["An obsolete map leading into a closed works zone invalidates precise distance calculations.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted."],"answer":0,"explanation":"舊版逃生圖若仍指向施工封閉段，距離計算再精確也無效。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An obsolete map leading into a closed works zone invalidates precise distance calculations. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b104-v14-37","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-36"],"objective":"說明「資產資料完整度」如何影響勒奇山基線隧道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Asset-record completeness” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Lotschberg Base Tunnel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"擴建介面需把舊設備識別碼、控制位址與新竣工資料連結，檢查維修系統是否能辨認同名不同孔設備。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「資產資料完整度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Link legacy identifiers and control addresses to expansion records, testing whether maintenance systems distinguish similarly named assets in different bores. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision. Drawings without change history cannot distinguish replacement from deterioration. Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asset-record completeness” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創教學假設：設備總數=103 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=103 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.466 %.","failure":"常見誤解：「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「資產資料完整度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asset-record completeness”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-37-k1","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover","text":"擴建介面需把舊設備識別碼、控制位址與新竣工資料連結，檢查維修系統是否能辨認同名不同孔設備。地下設備的竣工資料必須讓維護人員找到正確位置、材料批次和控制版本。","textEn":"Link legacy identifiers and control addresses to expansion records, testing whether maintenance systems distinguish similarly named assets in different bores. Handover must let maintainers find the correct location, material batch and control revision.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" is correct?","options":["全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。","擴建介面需把舊設備識別碼、控制位址與新竣工資料連結，檢查維修系統是否能辨認同名不同孔設備。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.","Link legacy identifiers and control addresses to expansion records, testing whether maintenance systems distinguish similarly named assets in different bores.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"擴建介面需把舊設備識別碼、控制位址與新竣工資料連結，檢查維修系統是否能辨認同名不同孔設備。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Link legacy identifiers and control addresses to expansion records, testing whether maintenance systems distinguish similarly named assets in different bores. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b104-v14-38","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「資產資料完整度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Asset-record completeness” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設：設備總數=103 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.466 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.9126 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions: asset count=103 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.466 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.9126 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：抽樣由現場標籤追到圖紙、控制點及檢修紀錄。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Sample the trace from field label to drawing, control point and maintenance record.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創教學假設：設備總數=103 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.466 %。僅把缺紀錄數增加10%，其他條件不變，重算為82.9126 %。邊界：資料完整度，不等於安全或可靠度；擾動為連續敏感度，實際個數為整數；不是本工程實測或允收值。","textEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=103 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.466 %. Increasing only missing records by 10% with all other inputs fixed gives 82.9126 %. Boundary: Record completeness, not safety or reliability; perturbation is continuous sensitivity while actual counts are integers. These are not project measurements or acceptance values.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「資產編碼與可追溯交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Asset identity and traceable handover\", which statement holds?","options":["基線隧道坡度很小，所以不必做牽引與制動分析。","支護越厚越硬就一定能解決所有擠壓性地層。","原創教學假設：設備總數=103 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。"],"optionsEn":["A small base-tunnel gradient eliminates the need for traction and braking analysis.","Thicker and stiffer support necessarily solves every squeezing-ground problem.","Original teaching assumptions: asset count=103 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.466 %."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創教學假設：設備總數=103 個；缺紀錄數=16 個。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original teaching assumptions: asset count=103 count; missing records=16 count. coverage=100(N−missing)/N=84.466 %. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b104-v14-39","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「資產資料完整度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Asset-record completeness” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"抽樣由現場標籤追到圖紙、控制點及檢修紀錄。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Sample the trace from field label to drawing, control point and maintenance record. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽樣由現場標籤追到圖紙、控制點及檢修紀錄。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","observationEn":"Site practice: For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample the trace from field label to drawing, control point and maintenance record. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","failure":"注意干擾：重複識別碼會把故障回報派到錯誤孔別，完整表格也可能內容錯配。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Duplicate identifiers send fault responses to the wrong bore despite apparently complete records. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"抽樣由現場標籤追到圖紙、控制點及檢修紀錄。抽取一條告警，從控制畫面追到設備、線路、圖面和工單，核對位置、版本及校正日期並記錄無法閉合的欄位。比對時保留校正、時間與基準版本，允收採設計核准條件。","textEn":"Sample the trace from field label to drawing, control point and maintenance record. Trace a sampled alarm from screen to equipment, circuit, drawing and work order, checking location, revision and calibration dates and recording broken links. Retain calibration, timing and datum revisions, and compare against design-approved conditions.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"本案「資產資料完整度」的交付需回答：抽樣由現場標籤追到圖紙、控制點及檢修紀錄。交接以可完成的定位、查找與復原任務驗證，由維護責任人確認現場可用性；完整度只是資料指標，不代表結構安全或設備可靠。","textEn":"For Lotschberg Base Tunnel, the asset-record completeness handover must address the following evidence: Sample the trace from field label to drawing, control point and maintenance record. Validate handover through achievable location, retrieval and recovery tasks witnessed by maintainers; completeness measures records, not structural safety or equipment reliability.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「資產編碼與可追溯交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Asset identity and traceable handover\"?","options":["抽樣由現場標籤追到圖紙、控制點及檢修紀錄。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩次閉合結果一致就能證明地下控制網沒有系統誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Sample the trace from field label to drawing, control point and maintenance record.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two matching closures prove that an underground network has no systematic error."],"answer":0,"explanation":"抽樣由現場標籤追到圖紙、控制點及檢修紀錄。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Sample the trace from field label to drawing, control point and maintenance record. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b104-v14-40","title":"資產編碼與可追溯交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Asset identity and traceable handover: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"prerequisiteIds":["b104-v14-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「資產資料完整度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Asset-record completeness” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"重複識別碼會把故障回報派到錯誤孔別，完整表格也可能內容錯配。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Duplicate identifiers send fault responses to the wrong bore despite apparently complete records. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：只有上傳圖面而沒有變更歷程，無法分辨元件替換與真正劣化；告警、儀器、線路及工單使用一致識別碼，才可能把量測趨勢連回實際受力或水力系統。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Consistent identifiers across alarms, instruments, circuits and work orders are essential for linking trends to the physical structural or hydraulic system instead of treating each record as an isolated file.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「全部檔案上傳完成就代表工程交接已經驗收合格。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Uploading all files means that engineering handover has been accepted.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b104-v14-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"重複識別碼會把故障回報派到錯誤孔別，完整表格也可能內容錯配。設備改名卻未更新控制畫面會引導人員隔離錯誤回路，材料批次缺漏則使同批缺陷無法追蹤到其他位置。","textEn":"Duplicate identifiers send fault responses to the wrong bore despite apparently complete records. Renaming an asset without updating the screen can isolate the wrong circuit; missing material batches prevent tracing related defects at other locations.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]},{"id":"b104-v14-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「資產編碼與可追溯交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Asset identity and traceable handover\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","重複識別碼會把故障回報派到錯誤孔別，完整表格也可能內容錯配。","最短的隧道路線一定也有最低施工與維護風險。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Duplicate identifiers send fault responses to the wrong bore despite apparently complete records.","The shortest tunnel alignment necessarily has the lowest construction and maintenance risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"重複識別碼會把故障回報派到錯誤孔別，完整表格也可能內容錯配。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Duplicate identifiers send fault responses to the wrong bore despite apparently complete records. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v14s-landmark-b104","b-src-underground","v14s-landmark-piarc"],"curriculumVersion":14,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
